# Datetime bodies are checked with precise spans.
mode: syntax
---- query
from datetime(2023-02-29) datetime(2024-13-01) datetime(now())
---- expected
PROGRAM@0..63
  PIPELINE@0..62
    IDENT@0..4 "from"
    WHITESPACE@4..5 " "
    LITERAL@5..25
      DATETIME@5..25 "datetime(2023-02-29)"
    WHITESPACE@25..26 " "
    ERROR@26..62
      DATETIME@26..46 "datetime(2024-13-01)"
      WHITESPACE@46..47 " "
      DATETIME@47..61 "datetime(now()"
      R_PAREN@61..62 ")"
  WHITESPACE@62..63 "\n"

error[DS0003]: invalid datetime `2023-02-29`
  --> query:1:23
  |
1 | from datetime(2023-02-29) datetime(2024-13-01) datetime(now())
  |                       ^^ February 2023 has 28 days
  |
  = help: write an ISO 8601 date: `datetime(2024-01-31)` or `datetime(2024-01-31T12:00:00Z)`

error[DS0101]: expected `|` or `;`, found `datetime(2024-13-01)`
  --> query:1:27
  |
1 | from datetime(2023-02-29) datetime(2024-13-01) datetime(now())
  |                           ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^

error[DS0003]: invalid datetime `2024-13-01`
  --> query:1:41
  |
1 | from datetime(2023-02-29) datetime(2024-13-01) datetime(now())
  |                                         ^^ months are 01 to 12
  |
  = help: write an ISO 8601 date: `datetime(2024-01-31)` or `datetime(2024-01-31T12:00:00Z)`

error[DS0003]: invalid datetime `now(`
  --> query:1:57
  |
1 | from datetime(2023-02-29) datetime(2024-13-01) datetime(now())
  |                                                         ^^^^ not a date
  |
  = help: write an ISO 8601 date: `datetime(2024-01-31)` or `datetime(2024-01-31T12:00:00Z)`
  = help: to convert a value to a datetime, use `todatetime(...)`
